---
const faqs = [
  {
    q: "Do I need an answer key?",
    a: "No. Matdo checks completed work from the questions and answers on your pages. There is no answer key to upload and no assignment to create."
  },
  {
    q: "Why not just use ChatGPT?",
    a: "<p>You certainly can. But Matdo is built for one job: checking finished homework.</p>"
      + "<ul>"
      + "<li><b>Take a photo, and we do the rest.</b> No answer key, no prompts, nothing to type. We’re parents too, and we know how long checking homework takes.</li>"
      + "<li><b>Marks on the paper.</b> See right on the page which answers need another look, without going back and forth between a chat and the worksheet.</li>"
      + "<li><b>Step-by-step explanations</b> that help you help your child, not just hand over answers.</li>"
      + "<li><b>Made for parents.</b> A simple app built around homework, not a chat window.</li>"
      + "</ul>"
      + "<p>Like any AI, Matdo can make mistakes, so give the marks a quick look.</p>"
  },
  {
    q: "What kinds of homework can it check?",
    a: 'Handwritten math, science and reading work, plus written feedback on essays. Matdo reads your child’s handwriting, and with <strong>Multi-page</strong> it can check a worksheet that runs over several pages, including a passage or instructions on another page. See the <a href="#samples">real checked pages</a> above.'
  },
  {
    q: "What if a result seems wrong?",
    a: "Open the details to compare what Matdo read with the paper, next to the correct answer and explanation. If messy handwriting or a missing page threw it off, take a clearer photo or add the page and check again, or use <strong>Regrade</strong> on the same pages. Each new check uses units like the first."
  },
  {
    q: "Is my child’s homework kept private?",
    a: 'Your pages go through our server to Google’s AI for checking. Matdo Lab does not keep a copy of the pages or results unless you send us a problem report, and neither we nor Google use them to train AI models. Saved checks stay on your device; delete them anytime in <strong>Previous Grading</strong>. See the <a href="/privacy/grade">privacy policy</a> for details.'
  },
];
---
<section id="grade-faq" class="section-pad grade-faq" aria-labelledby="grade-faq-title">
  <div class="wrap faq-wrap">
    <div class="sec-head center reveal">
      <h2 id="grade-faq-title">A few questions before you start</h2>
      <p>How paper homework, explanations and saved work fit together.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="faq-list">
      {faqs.map(faq => <details><summary>{faq.q}</summary><div class="faq-answer" set:html={faq.a} /></details>)}
    </div>
    <p class="faq-support">Need more detail? <a href="/support/grade">Read the support guide</a> or <a href="/contact">contact Matdo Lab</a>.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .faq-wrap { max-width: 900px; }
  .faq-list { border-top: 1px solid var(--color-line); }
  details { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-line); }
  summary { padding: 22px 8px; cursor: pointer; font-weight: 600; color: var(--color-forest); min-height: 48px; }
  summary:focus-visible { outline: 3px solid var(--color-mint); outline-offset: 3px; border-radius: 12px; }
  .faq-answer { padding: 0 8px 24px; color: #4a5854; }
  /* Answers with paragraphs or a list (most are a single plain sentence block). */
  .faq-answer :global(p) { margin: 0 0 0.6rem; }
  .faq-answer :global(p:last-child) { margin-bottom: 0; }
  .faq-answer :global(ul) { list-style: disc; padding-left: 1.3rem; margin: 0 0 0.6rem; }
  .faq-answer :global(li) { margin: 0.35rem 0; }
  .faq-answer :global(b) { color: var(--color-forest); }
  .faq-answer :global(a), .faq-support a { color: var(--color-teal); text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 3px; }
  .faq-support { margin: 1.5rem 0 0; color: #4a5854; }
</style>
